==Battleground==
*3 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Maawth]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*8 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cosmic Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**12 [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
**1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Even though this stage only requires [[Into the Future]] Chapter 1 to be beaten, it is highly recommended to have all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from all three chapters before attempting it.

The main threat is the Cosmic Cyclone, so bring [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] and optionally [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] in order to keep it frozen/slowed, and be careful not to knock it back into Galactic Overseer Nyandam's range. Make sure to bring a heavy hitter and at least one cheap attacker in order to deal with the Imperator Saels and Kroxos.

==Trivia==
*Space is the Place's Japanese name, Uchū Sensō (宇宙戦争, "Space War"), is also the Japanese name of [[wikipedia:The War of the Worlds|''The War of the Worlds'']], a sci-fi novel about an alien invasion.
*[[wikipedia:Space is the Place|Space Is the Place]] is a sci-fi film released in 1974, directed by John Coney and written by Sun Ra and Joshua Smith.

